        "articleNumber": "5007334",
        "articleTitle": "A Binary Outscriber using Facsimile Paper",
        "volume": "PGI-2",
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "65",
        "endPage": "73",
        "publisher": "IEEE",
        "articleContentType": "Journals",
        "publicationTitle": "Transactions of the IRE Professional Group on Instrumentation",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": 37313001200,
                "preferredName": "Willis H. Ware",
                "firstName": "Willis H.",
                "lastName": "Ware"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "In summary, there has been described an Outscriber which, using a modified Western Union 3-stylus Teledeltos recorder in conjunction with the required accessory electronic and mechanical equipment, is capable of printing, in a binary presentation, 80,000 bits per minute. The record is in the form of two 40-bit words per line, and 1000 lines per minute. Each line of data may, if desired, be reprinted up to 8 consecutive times in order to give immunity against statistical fluctuations in the paper characteristics and in the operation of the device. A record containing 1,024 words, where each of the 512 lines has been printed one time, is included on a piece of Teledeltos paper 8-1/4'' by 19''. After there is deducted from this area of paper the 1-5/8'' of width for the edge and center margins, the figure of merit for this device is found to be 320 bits per square inch per unit time.",
